diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..3f2be0c 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -159,3 +159,40 @@ __Response:__
 ```
 
 `request` and `response` can be `null` for deliveries that have not started yet or are still in progress. The delivery request headers omit the `X-Webhook-Signature` header.
+
+## Delivery format
+
+When a subscribed event happens on the board, Fizzy sends a `POST` request to the webhook's URL with a JSON body describing the event. The `eventable` is the card or comment the event is about, and `board` and `creator` use the same shape as elsewhere in the API. Abbreviated example:
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohde",
+  "action": "card_closed",
+  "created_at": "2025-12-05T19:36:35.401Z",
+  "eventable": {
+    "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohdb",
+    "number": 1,
+    "title": "Fix the login page",
+    "status": "published",
+    "closed": true,
+    "url": "http://app.fizzy.localhost:3006/897362094/cards/1"
+  },
+  "board": { "id": "03f5v9zkfs4hj9qq0lsn9ohcy", "name": "Fizzy" },
+  "creator": { "id": "03f5v9zjw7pz8717a4no1h8a7", "name": "David Heinemeier Hansson" }
+}
+```
+
+Each request includes these headers:
+
+- `User-Agent: fizzy/1.0.0 Webhook`
+- `Content-Type: application/json`
+- `X-Webhook-Timestamp`: the time the event happened, in ISO 8601 with milliseconds.
+- `X-Webhook-Signature`: the hex-encoded HMAC-SHA256 of the raw request body, keyed with the webhook's signing secret. Compare it against a digest you compute to confirm the request came from Fizzy.
+
+__Delivery rules:__
+
+- Each event is sent once to each subscribed webhook. Failed deliveries are not retried.
+- Respond with a `2xx` status. Fizzy waits up to 10 seconds for a response. Redirects are not followed, so any other status counts as a failure.
+- The URL must resolve to a public IP address. Requests to private, loopback, or link-local addresses are never sent.
+- After 10 consecutive failed deliveries, where the failures began at least an hour earlier, Fizzy deactivates the webhook. Reactivate it with `POST /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks/:id/activation`. Reactivation starts a new failure count.
+- Delivery history (see the deliveries endpoint above) is kept for one week.
